<content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Compare each of the following graphs, then list a reason for each graph why it would not belong with the other three.</para>
<para>Graph A.</para>
<media><image alt="Graph of two intersecting lines." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/339700bb45cf8d4d0f0e4c34e60b513a91b510a2"/></media><para>Graph B.</para>
<media><image alt="Graph of 2 inequalities." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/1b08cc9603bc374c60231ff673d72f1f3c36a589"/></media><para>Graph C.</para>
<media><image alt="Graph of two inequalities." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/2b47a1c41ffec0e0eb3f04aa60993434993e9d5d"/></media><para>Graph D.</para>
<media><image alt="Graph of line, no grid, origin O.  Each axis from negative 10 to 10, by 5's. The line passes through negative 10 comma 10, 0 comma 0, 5 comma negative 5. The region above the line is shaded.  " src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8774d694cf4a97291b5f8660e8a7ee0b321b1bc6"/></media><exercise>
  <problem>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <div class="body">Enter your answer here:</div>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Your answers may vary,, but here are some samples.</para>
    <list>
      <item>Graph  A is the only set of graphs that represents a system of equations. It is the only system with exactly one solution. </item>
      <item>Graph  B is the only set of graphs that represents a system of inequalities with no solutions. </item>
      <item>Graph  C is the only set of graphs in which the boundaries are horizontal and vertical lines. It is the only one representing a system with an infinite number of solutions. </item>
      <item>Graph  D is the only graph that does not represent a system. It only represents one inequality.</item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise></section>
</content>
